  SPCX [negative]: SpaceX (SPCX) shares fell on November 5 and extended declines into November 6, as Wall Street weighed possible regulatory hurdles after the Democratic midterm sweep. Reports also said AT&T and T-Mobile have discussed removing Boost Mobile from their networks if SpaceX acquires the EchoStar unit, and the broader market sell-off spread beyond AI stocks.
  PLTR [negative]: Palantir reported 96% revenue growth, its fastest in its public company history, yet the stock still fell as investors sold off tech and AI names amid a broader sell-off. As of Nov 6 it traded at $161.69, up 4.32% intraday, though one outlet describes the daily trend as still weak.

